 ### [Sigma-Threshold Depth Rendering](5955-sigma-threshold-depth-rendering.md)
-Sigma-Threshold Depth Rendering computes a binary mask indicating the sample index where cumulative weight accumulation exceeds a specified density threshold, effectively identifying a 'surface' location along the ray. It serves as a differentiable depth estimation method that renders a binary or thresholded output based on whether volume density exceeds a given value, referencing the approach used in Dex-NeRF. Unlike Expected Term Rendering which computes the mean distance, or Median Depth Rendering which finds the median, this method identifies the depth at which the accumulated opacity crosses a hard boundary. It builds on [Depth from Ray Distance](5665-depth-from-ray-distance.md) by introducing a termination condition based on accumulated sigma rather than fixed sample counts or probabilistic expectations [G].
